      "content": "For a 4-year-old boy weighing 38lbs, the maximum safe dosage of acetaminophen for infants is generally 10-15mg per kg of body weight, taken every 4-6 hours as needed. Calculating this accurately for your son:\n\n10-15mg/kg * 38kgs = 380-570mg (since we gave an example of using the adult dosage of 160mg, it is approximately 287mg/kg if we use this ratio)\n\nTo find out the corresponding milliliters (mL) for the 160mg of adult acetaminophen:\n\n160mg / 287mg per 5ml = 0.5577\n\nSo,\n\n0.5577 * 5 = 2.79mL (approximately)\n\nTherefore, to give him 160mg of acetaminophen as per the dosage found from the adult version, measure approximately 2.8 mL using a syringe.\n\nFor a 4-year-old weighing 38lbs, it's better to proceed with caution and strictly follow the vet's suggestions considering the weight. You would need to adjust this to the recommended safe dosage, and if you have any doubts, consult a professional later.\n\nAlways measure carefully, ideally use a syringe",
